{"ts": "2026-10-28T21:56:40.497877Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T2156Z-19b4", "unit": "openspec:add-oidc-login", "seq": 9, "type": "task.started", "task": "4.1", "title": "4.1 Write `src/identity/oidc/client.test.ts` first (`startFakeOidc({ now })` with a mutable `Clock`; injected `fetch` doubles for the hostile cases, each also asserting `init.redirect === \"error\"` and an `init.signal`; scenarios \"Cached and refetched once\", \"Hostile answers\" and \"Code exchange\"; the code comes from `completeFakeLogin(fake, url, \"alice\")` for an authorization URL the test builds with its own state, nonce and S256 challenge), then implement `completeFakeLogin` in `test/support/oidc-login.ts` (it `fetch`es `authorizationUrl` with `redirect: \"manual\"`, reads the form `action` (unescaping `&amp;`, resolving against the URL), POSTs `username` and `fake.passwordOf(username)` form-encoded and returns the `Location` of the 302, throwing an `Error` when there is none) and `createOidcClient` in `src/identity/oidc/client.ts`: `fetch` (injected or global) with `redirect: \"error\"`, `AbortSignal.timeout(timeoutMs ?? 5000)` and a 262144-byte cap read from the body stream; a network error, timeout, oversize, 5xx or non-JSON answer is `OidcError` `OIDC_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE`; discovery from `issuer + \"/.well-known/openid-configuration\"` whose `issuer` equals the configured one and whose `authorization_endpoint`, `token_endpoint`, `jwks_uri` are URLs of the issuer's origin (`end_session_endpoint` too, else `logoutUrl` is `null`), cached 3600 s of `clock`; `signingKey(kid)` from the JWKS cached the same way, one refetch on an unknown `kid`, keeping only `kty` `RSA` keys of at least 2048 bits with `use` absent or `sig` and `alg` absent or `RS256`, dropping every key whose `kid` repeats, at most 32; `exchangeCode(code, codeVerifier, redirectUri)` POSTs `grant_type=authorization_code&code&redirect_uri&code_verifier` form-encoded with `Authorization: Basic base64(urlencode(clientId):urlencode(secret))` and returns the string `id_token`; a 4xx answer or no string `id_token` is `OIDC_EXCHANGE_FAILED`; no error holds a URL or body, implementing requirement \"The provider client is cached, bounded and confined to the issuer\""}
